@using MartenStudio.Services.Database

@*
    The Rows tab's slot. ObjectDetail renders this only when the service said the relation's rows may be
    read (DatabaseRelationSummary.Rows.Allowed); every refusal - Marten's own tables, a foreign table, a view
    over a hidden type, a gate that is shut - is drawn by the page before it gets here.

    A placeholder until the row grid lands, and deliberately a component with a fixed signature rather than
    markup inline in the page: the grid replaces this file, the page does not change, and the parameters
    below are the whole contract between the two.

      Schema  - the relation's schema, as the catalog spells it
      Name    - the relation's name, likewise
      Detail  - the DatabaseObjectDetail the page already read (columns, row key, keys both ways), typed
                object for the reason DocumentComponentModel gives
*@

<div class="ms-empty ms-db-rows-slot" data-schema="@Schema" data-name="@Name">
    <p class="ms-empty-title">Rows</p>
    <p class="ms-empty-description">
        @if (DetailModel?.Relation is { } relation)
        {
            <text>
                @(relation.EstimatedRows is { } rows ? "About " + DatabasePresentation.Number(rows) + " rows" : "An unknown number of rows")
                can be read here@(DetailModel.RowKey is { } key ? ", one at a time by (" + string.Join(", ", key.Columns) + ")" : string.Empty).
            </text>
        }
        The row grid is not part of this build yet; the structure tabs beside this one are.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The relation's schema.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Schema { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The relation's name.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The relation's <c>DatabaseObjectDetail</c>. Typed <see cref="object" /> - see <c>DocumentComponentModel</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public object? Detail { get; set; }

    private DatabaseObjectDetail? DetailModel => Detail as DatabaseObjectDetail;
}
